e some kind of history  academic or something like i really i  live for it um and so to do any kind of  period piece is just such a joy to kind  of do all the research and get your you  know really um involve yourself in that  world as much as you possibly can i  really get off on it um  to work on german jack was amazing yeah  sally wayne wright the writer is you  know my one of my favorite writers of  all time her work on tv  in the uk is just incredible and saran  jones is just amazing in the series it's  an incredible story as well and it's a  story that's i've so i'm from yorkshire  um in the uk and um and it's where it's  it's where the story is based and so to  go up you know i was able to like stay  at my parents house as we were shooting  and so it was amazing and it's the first  job i ever really got i got it straight  out of drama school and so it was just  you know throwing it at the deep end  because it's incred you've seen the  series haven't you yeah it's an  incredible character and so it was just  it was such a joy to um to finally play  but it's yeah very very different from  this much darker even though this this  story of this film is incredibly dark  it's a very it's a yeah it's a dark  what what what do you learn about acting  and about the craft of acting after  doing something like that after doing  this i mean you're still sort of so new  to the whole thing how different did you  feel as an actor now  i mean i feel a lot more confident i'm  like really ready and raring to go for  the next thing like i i really really am  i think i was worried i'm not worried in  a sense but you know i come from i can i  drama school training and i come from a  very like theatrical background and so  that's what i was used to is movies are  very different and it's it's a whole  different way you know acting is acting  but you know the way of you know making  sure the camera and stuff it's all very  it's a different method of working and  so i i feel like i actually love it more  than i thought i would i just might i'd  love to just do you know maybe for the  rest of my life it's it's that kind of  thing of you know you have three months  to just get your head down and you're  just you're on location the whole time  and you're just it's all about the work  that you're creating with other creative  people and it's it's like that's your  one job it's your one prerogative let's  just get this one script down and and to  be so  like to go so in depth with one piece  you know rather than like an eight  episode thing where you're kind of  having to think you've got you so many  different balls to juggle on tv i think  um with filmmaking it's um  the focus is a lot stronger  and i really like that way of working  it's much more um it's much more my  style i think i don't know what it comes  across in the film  a lot of actors i've talked to talk  about you know wanting to play roles  that scare them yes  get a sense of that yourself i mean  totally yeah i mean and that can come in  it  yeah definitely that can come in many  many ways you know a challenge is  is is a challenge for many different  reasons it doesn't have to be you know i  think people kind of want to go you know  i play a crazy character who does loads  of crazy stuff but actually like a  challenge can be in like an intimate  scene with somebody where it's just you  two in a room talking and finding out  what you want from each other um  a challenge can come you know in in  terms of different parts i this was a  big challenge for me because i felt a  lot of pressure is the only kind of  british  actor with you know a huge american and  south african team like i you know the  accent was i just wanted to like really  nail the accent and you know the loads  of different pressures your fight  training and horse riding training it  was you know it was a big  it was a big leap but um  hopefully i did it justice we'll just  find out yeah  oh you pulled it off so thank you good  thank you  thank you for talking to me about it i  appreciate it i thoroughly enjoyed the  movies thank you so much really nice to  meet you yeah
 

